EXERCISE 8
Build visualizations in Power BI using charts, tables, and slicers with proper formatting
Objective
To design clear, interactive, and well-formatted visuals using charts, tables, and slicers.
Procedure
Step 1: Create a Table Visual
Go to Report View.
Click the Table icon from the Visualizations pane.
Drag the following fields:
Product Name
Year
Total Sales
Total Profit
Step 2: Create a Bar / Column Chart
Click the Clustered Column Chart icon.
Drag:
Axis → Product Category / Region
Values → Total Sales
Resize the chart appropriately.
Step 3: Create a Line Chart
Click the Line Chart icon.
Drag:
X-Axis → Year or Order Date
Y-Axis → Total Sales
Enable Data Labels if required.
Step 4: Add Slicers
Click the Slicer visual.
Drag Year or Region into the slicer.
Change slicer type (Dropdown / List) from Format pane.
Step 5: Apply Formatting
Select any visual.
Open Format pane (paint roller icon).



Apply:
Title and alignment
Font size and color
Data labels
Background and border
Ensure consistency across all visuals.
Step 6: Enable Visual Interaction
Select a chart.
Click Format → Edit Interactions.
Confirm visuals cross-filter correctly.
Expected Output
Interactive charts and tables
Working slicers controlling all visuals
Properly formatted, readable dashboard


Result
Clear and interactive Power BI visuals are successfully created using charts, tables, and slicers.

